# No host software installs

Never install software on the user's machine. Never attempt it. Never ask for approval to run an installer as a workaround.

Forbidden examples:

- `winget`, `choco`, `scoop`, `brew`, `apt`, `msiexec`, setup/installer executables
- Global package installs (`npm i -g`, `bun add -g`, `pip install --user`, `cargo install`)
- Downloading CLIs or binaries into system or user-bin paths
- `rustup` toolchain or component installs, unless the user explicitly asked for that exact command

If a tool is missing, stop. Tell the user which command failed and which already-installed tool is required. Do not suggest or run an install command.

Allowed: project-local dependencies in this repository (`bun add`, `cargo add`) that follow the 2-day quarantine rule. Use only tools that are already on PATH.
